HOL4 conditional/contextual simplifier
======================================

Ordinary develop clients need no migration. Use simpLib/congLib, Traverse,
pureSimps/boolSimps/combinSimps as before. Ordinary loads do not import the
extension engine, strategy state, source inventories or split persistence.

Extension clients use simpExtLib/TraverseExt types; ordinary fragments and
simpsets enter by simpExtLib.lift_ssfrag/lift_simpset. Configured congruence
uses congExtLib; threaded factories are Opening.THREADED_CONGPROC and
Travrules.mk_threaded_travrules; paired conditional compilation uses
Cond_rewrExt. Both engines share TraverseCore, congLibFn and simpCommon.

Current documentation and ownership:
  src/notes.md                           migration, controls, rebuild caveats
  src/MANIFEST                           defining modules and dependency rules
  tests/api-audit/Documentation.sml       executable typed examples
  tests/simp-ext/APIExamples.sml          configured/global tactic examples
  help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.*.smd          extension reference (repository root)

From the repository root:
  bin/Holmake --holstate="$PWD/bin/hol.state0" \
    -C src/simp/src -j1 HOLSELFTESTLEVEL=1 all

Ordinary selftest.sml does not import the extension engine. Extension tests,
public source clients and fresh-load/persistence fixtures have independent
processes and normal-level targets. After list theories are built, the
normal build sequence runs tests/native-extension again, including the
option/pair/list cases that the earlier run skips.

Persistent [split] declarations require explicit splitPersistLib loading and
Theory.add_ML_dependency "splitPersistLib" on the earliest declaring theory.
Rebuild old mixed-branch extension theories, ML products and saved heaps from
scripts; ordinary develop source clients and generic markers are unchanged.
